  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Showers and thunderstorms possible this afternoon, \nsome of which may produce strong gusty winds and heavy rainfall.  \n\nThe potential for showers and thunderstorms will increase this \nafternoon as the low over the northern Ontario Province send a cold \nfront through the region. Little overall change with previous \nthinking as guidance continues to show a low CAPE/high shear (+40) \nenvironment. Latest CAMS continuing to suggest a line of storms \npushing into the area between 18Z-21Z this afternoon with the front. \nCAPE values do not look overly impressive due to morning showers and \ncloud cover. Despite the lack of instability, given the decent shear \nstorms will have the potential to become strong to severe with the \nprimary risk damaging wind gusts. SPC has highlighted our region in \na Slight Risk for severe storms. Additionally...PWATs will be found \nin the 1.5-1.75\" range ahead of the cold front. If storms were to \ntrain over the same location the heavy rainfall may cause localized \nflash flooding. There continues to be a Marginal Risk for excessive \nrainfall, with an expansion of the Slight Risk area across Jefferson \nand far northern Lewis county.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Dry Weather returns Monday and notably cooler.  \n\nShowers and storms will end from NW to SE this evening and tonight \nbehind the front, with a much cooler air mass spilling in across the \nLower Lakes. With high pressure building in Monday expect dry \nweather but cool conditions as H850 T's dip into the single digits.",
